  "problem": "$(-63)÷(-9)=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We have to divide a negative number $(-63)$ by another negative number $(-9).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-63)÷(-9)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $63$ by $9$ without any signs: $63÷9=7.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-63)÷(-9)=7.\n$$",
